Name: Remove skirt and surround(as needed) to allow access to motion base for maintenance and cleaning. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Run machine and observe for  gearmotor brake for chatter, wear and loose looking bearings | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Inspect and test the functionality and alignment of all safety switches on the exterior of the machine.  (*Lower Door Limit  *Upper Door Limit  )" | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Be sure to turn off power and "LOCKOUT" the machine before performing any maintenance to mechanical systems. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check tightness of capsule and motion base bolts | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check gearmotor assemblies for wear and bolt tightness | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check universal joint and main center column. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Flag;
Name: "One pump from the grease gun to the  following grease fittings.  Also grease rod end bearings as needed (4) -pillow blocks              (2) - Universal Joint      (1/2) center column   (3) - gearmotors (if applicable)" | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: With a rag remove the excess grease from all bearings and greasing points. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check operation and security of Main Disconnect Switch. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Thoroughly vacuum all electronic components on the entire machine including drives, wiring harnesses, etc.  Vacuum motion base during this step also. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Inspect control rack wiring to make sure all connections are secure and that all wiring is neatly routed. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Inspect all control rack components to be sure that everything is secure and all screws are in place. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check encoders for wear/damage, security and function. (if external encoders check the coupler security and alignment) | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Inspect and vacuum AC condenser and check wiring and hoses. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Fail;
Name: Ensure all cables/wires are clear of moving parts and foot traffic. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check Capsule to Motion Base Securing bolts | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Remove Nose access panel | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Visually inspect capsule wiring for loose and frayed wires. Make sure all wiring & harnesses are secure. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Clean projection mirror and screen(backside) and check for issues. If applicable | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Visually inspect the condition of the capsule interior for poor housekeeping, damage/wear and sharp objects that could injure patrons. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Remove rear seat and service/clean/vacuum AC air handler (if applicable).  | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Replace nose access panel and rear seat. Vacuum and wipe down capsule interior as needed. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Replace skirt and surround | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Test all ESTOPs (passenger and operator for proper operations) | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
