Name: Review Weekly Morphis Maintenance Checklists. (Attach pictures of weekly sheets to this item using the attachment or camera button to the right) | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Flag;
Name: Be sure to turn off power and "LOCKOUT" the machine before performing any maintenance to mechanical systems. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check tightness of capsule and motion base bolts | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Drain the air and clean the compressor and filters | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Change/clean air blower inlet filter element (if applicable) | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Clean oil cooler and change/clean cooler filter (if applicable) | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check motion base and HPU hydraulics for leaks | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Flag;
Name: Clean/vacuum/dust motion base as needed | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: "One pump from the grease gun to the  following grease fittings.   (4) - linear bearing assembly           (4) - universal joint assembly     (4) - fittings fixed pivot bearing assemblies (if applicable)" | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: With a rag remove the excess grease from all bearings and greasing points. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Ensure all hoses and electrical looms are clear of moving parts. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check Main Power Disconnect Switch. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Inspect control rack wiring to make sure all connections are secure and that all wiring is neatly routed. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Inspect all control rack components to be sure that everything is secure and all screws are in place. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Thoroughly vacuum all electronic components | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Turn on/startup the system and allow air pressure to build/doors to open | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Thoroughly vacuum the interior of the capsule being sure to remove dust from capsule wiring harnesses , fans, projector housing, projector and filter. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Visually inspect capsule wiring for loose and frayed wires. Make sure all wiring & harnesses are secure. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Visually inspect handrails for signs of wear and security. Ensure all fasteners are tight | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Clean the projector screen | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Visually inspect the condition of the capsule interior for poor housekeeping and damaged upholstery. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check security of AC unit.  Inspect for anything sharp and for damage to mount. Vacuum Air handler and condenser. Inspect hoses for damage and security. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Flag;
Name: Visually inspect the capsule interior for any sharp surfaces that could injure patrons. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check air pressure regulator for correct pressure | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Inspect and test the functionality door switches | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Inspect and test the functionality of all E-Stop buttons. (*Rack  *Capsule) | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Test run the machine | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Please record any issues that need to be addressed whether related to equipment, reporting, or house keeping and submit a Support Request for any outstanding issues.  (You must enter something in this box to complete the maintenance) | Type: Text Form Item | Value: Clean house keeping.;

Name: Ensure the weekly checklist is not past due, if so complete that first. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Grease the 12 upper and 8 lower grease fittings. Apply a general purpose grease 1 pump per fitting. Wipe off excess grease after competed. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Run a complete test ride to make sure system functions properly. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Disconnect electrical power to the air compressor. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check the compressor drive belts for tension. The belts should not move up and down while the compressor runs and when stopped should not have more than ½ inch of play when depressed. Be careful not to over tighten the belts during adjustment. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name:  Remove and inspect air compressor filters. Clean or replace filters as needed. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name:  Perform pre-operational checks and start a normal ride cycle.   Approximately half way through the ride cycle turn the main  power off to simulate a power failure. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: The capsule should slowly return to the rest or home position.  | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name:  Once the simulator has returned to the rest position test  the emergency valves on the air locker to open the door.  | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name:  Close the door, turn on electrical power and start up the system as per normal operating procedure. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name:  Lubricate door cylinder pivot points with a general purpose lubricating oil. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: If any issues were noted please create a support REQUEST in UpKeep regarding this issue. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Additional comments can be noted here. | Type: Text Form Item | Value: NEED MORE 3M OIL ABSORBANT PADS;

Name: Clean/Dust around all computers. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check the “free play” of the bench. With the machine in stopped and in-home position grasp the front of the machine (footrest) and push side to side with about 5 lbs. of pressure. There should be some (about 1 to 2 inches) free play.  Any excess movement or noises should be flagged and noted here. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Conduct a visual inspection of under the bench looking for any loose wires, air leaks, and any excessive ware. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check for the security of mounting bolts, making sure they are tight. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Run a test show listening for any unusual noises and to make sure the bench is running as designed. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Allow compressor to build pressure and ensure pressure holds at about 120 PSI. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Note any additional discrepancies found and attach pictures if applicable.  (You must enter something in this field, if no issues found then enter "none") | Type: Text Form Item | Value: n.a;
Name: Lightly grease fittings on all ball joints. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check for air leaks and reseat airlines if leaks are found. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Clean all excess grease that may have fallen from ball joints. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check that jam nuts on all rams are tight against the clevis. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Perform a visual inspection of all bench welds securing the benches to the floor for security and integrity. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Air Compressor-Empty the catch bottle from the Air dryer. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Air Compressor- Check oil level and add oil as required. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Air Compressor-Drain condensation from compressor tank. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Air Compressor-Check for air leaks and repair if noted. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Air Compressor-Clean or replace filters as needed. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: If any issues were noted please create a support REQUEST in UpKeep regarding this issue. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
