Name: FIRST STEP - FIND OUT THE DEVICE'S IP ADDRESS.  Start up PC3 and the HL2 as per normal  Once you've turned the device on - you will need to enter the device PIN to start - which is: 11 12 13  Then we need the Device's IP Address.  When the device is connected to the server, his will be visible in the Lower Right Corner of the Blue Start Screen .  It will be: 192.168.?? | Type: Text Form Item | Value: 192.168.1.21 ;
Name: STEP 2 - Open MOZILLA FIREFOX on PC3 / connect to the Windows Device Portal  You may need to escape out of the server screen after starting PC3, so as to return to the Desktop Screen.   Open Firefox Browser (if for some reason Firefox is not installed, Google Chrome will be fine).  In the browser window enter: http://192.168.XX(the last two digits of the IP address)   This will take you to the Windows Device Portal in the Browser Tab. | Type: Text Form Item | Value: 192.168.1.20;
Name: STEP 3 - Turn off Kiosk Mode  Within the Windows Device Portal - on the left column of drop-down options, click:  - System > - Kiosk Mode  Then unclick the box marked: Enable Kiosk Mode  In the top Right Corner, click the POWER button, and press RESTART | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: STEP 4 - Turning off the PIN on start up  When the device has restarted, enter the PIN again (last time!)  And touch the windows symbol on your wrist to bring up the Start Screen  From the start screen, click:  - Settings > - Accounts > - Sign-in options >  In the box marked Require sign-in, you'll just need to change the drop-down box to NEVER | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: STEP 5 - Turning Kiosk Mode Back On  Returning to the Windows Device Portal browser tab on PC3 - go back to:  - System > - Kiosk Mode  Now, you'll need to click the box marked: Enable Kiosk Mode  In the section below called Startup App - from the drop-down box select this file:  CriticalDistance_1.0.0.0_arm64_cfm0ts7tr1y16  (it will be the only file called Critical Distance there!)  Then, in the top Right Corner, click the POWER button, and press RESTART   The device should restart to the Critical Distance Start Screen and be ready for guests.  | Type: Task | Value: Complete;

