Name: Vacuum all carpet inside of barriers | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Clean all TV screens | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Clean ticket desk and plexiglass | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Dust all inside portals and reachable sections of large outside portal | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Vacuum out all fans on all VR computers | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Remove, vacuum off, and replace filter on control rack computer | Type: Task | Value: Complete;

Name: Review past completed weekly and monthly checklists in Upkeep to ensure they are being done. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check tightness of all motionbase hold down bolts. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check tightness of all capsule hold down bolts. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Visual inspection off all interior capsule components inspecting for damage and security including: Seats, handrails, doors, hinges, door actuators, projector and mounting, screen, carpeting, flooring... | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Inspect and adjust projector alignment as needed. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Visual inspection of capsule body. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Inspection of loading platform, stairs, handrails, and all hardware. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Thorough inspection of all electrical systems including looms and junction.  Ensure all electrical is neatly and securely routed and not showing signs of damage. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Thorough inspection of all pneumatic and hydraulic lines and fittings. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Thoroughly dust/blowout/wipe down all electrical enclosures and degrease and dust motion base | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Replace hydraulic filter. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Clean hydraulic cooling radiator. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Change compressor oil using 30wt non detergent compressor oil. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Change compressor air filter. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Inspect and adjust air compressor drive belt for tension should not be overly tight but less than 1/2 inch of deflection when pressed.  | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Startup system per normal operating instructions. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Perform emergency power loss test and make sure machine comes to reset and emergency door controls work as intended. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Reset system per normal operation | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Test run machine and test each ESTOP in the system for proper function. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: If any issues were noted please create a support REQUEST in UpKeep regarding this issue. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Additional comments can be noted here. | Type: Text Form Item | Value: remove 3 cables no need, and rearrange cables. Fixed cooler motor box ;

Name: Ensure the weekly checklist is not past due, if so complete that first. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Grease the 12 upper and 8 lower grease fittings. Apply a general purpose grease 1 pump per fitting. Wipe off excess grease after competed. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Run a complete test ride to make sure system functions properly. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Disconnect electrical power to the air compressor. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check the compressor drive belts for tension. The belts should not move up and down while the compressor runs and when stopped should not have more than ½ inch of play when depressed. Be careful not to over tighten the belts during adjustment. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name:  Remove and inspect air compressor filters. Clean or replace filters as needed. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name:  Perform pre-operational checks and start a normal ride cycle.   Approximately half way through the ride cycle turn the main  power off to simulate a power failure. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: The capsule should slowly return to the rest or home position.  | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name:  Once the simulator has returned to the rest position test  the emergency valves on the air locker to open the door.  | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name:  Close the door, turn on electrical power and start up the system as per normal operating procedure. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name:  Lubricate door cylinder pivot points with a general purpose lubricating oil. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: If any issues were noted please create a support REQUEST in UpKeep regarding this issue. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Additional comments can be noted here. | Type: Text Form Item | Value: NONE;

Name: Review Monthly ESP Maintenance Checklist | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Remove skirt and surround(as needed) to allow access to motion base for maintenance and cleaning. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Run machine and observe for  gearmotor brake for chatter, wear and loose looking bearings | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: "Inspect and test the functionality and alignment of all safety switches on the exterior of the machine.  (*Lower Door Limit  *Upper Door Limit  )" | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Be sure to turn off power and "LOCKOUT" the machine before performing any maintenance to mechanical systems. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check tightness of capsule and motion base bolts | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check gearmotor assemblies for wear and bolt tightness | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check universal joint and main center column. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check motion base and gearmotors for leaks.  | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check rod end bearings for proper function and tightness | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check encoders for wear/damage, security and function. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Ensure all cables/wires are clear of moving parts and foot traffic. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check Capsule to Motion Base Securing bolts | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: If brake chatter was noticed, adjust brake pad/pressure plate for proper air gap -authorized personnel only | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check gearmotor external encoder couplers for security and alignment (if applicable) | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: If any other loose bearings or assemblies where noticed during test then adjust and tighten as needed | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Grease and clean off excess grease (1 pump) from all motion base bearings (2 universal, 1 or 2 center column, 4 yaw restrictor pillow blocks, 1 yaw restrictor rod end, 6 tie rod end) * yaw restrictor and tie rod end bearings may require manual greasing with an acid brush if not fitted with grease fitting. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Visually inspect all motionbase and capsule looms and wiring harnesses for loose or frayed wires. Make sure all wiring & harnesses are secure. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Dust and Vacuum out all dust and debris from under motionbase including any coils or filters on any external air conditioners if applicable. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Remove front nose access panel to access capsule nose | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Inspect capsule nose wiring and TV or Projector mounting for security or damage | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Dust and Vacuum out all dust and debris from nose of capsule including any air filters for blowers if fitted as well as any filters or fans located on TV or Projector. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Re install front nose access panel | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Inspect Power Distribution enclosure and connections. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Vacuum/dust fans and interior/exterior of power distribution panel. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Inspect control rack wiring to make sure all connections are secure and that all wiring is neatly routed. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Vacuum/dust fans and interior/exterior of control rack. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Visually inspect the condition of the capsule interior for poor housekeeping, damage/wear or any sharp surfaces that could injure patrons. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check security of all interior panels, parts, handrails, seats, and visible wiring harnesses etc for security. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: For Systems that use pneumatic doors follow the next 6 instructions labeled "AIR SYS" | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: AIR SYS: Inspect compressor and Pneumatic assembly for condition | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Replace compressor oil (use only ROLOIL- SINCOM/32E) | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Clean/Change air intake filter and line filter element And Clean compressor of dust and dirt | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check filter reducer and parts for efficiency and condition | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check operation of safety valve | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Visually inspect all pneumatic connections for leaks including cylinder hoses at door cylinder | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Re install skirt and surround | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Startup and test Run Machine | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Test all ESTOPs (passenger and operator for proper operations) | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
