Name: Ensure the weekly checklist is not past due, if so complete that first. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Grease the 12 upper and 8 lower grease fittings. Apply a general purpose grease 1 pump per fitting. Wipe off excess grease after competed. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Run a complete test ride to make sure system functions properly. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Disconnect electrical power to the air compressor. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Check the compressor drive belts for tension. The belts should not move up and down while the compressor runs and when stopped should not have more than ½ inch of play when depressed. Be careful not to over tighten the belts during adjustment. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name:  Remove and inspect air compressor filters. Clean or replace filters as needed. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name:  Perform pre-operational checks and start a normal ride cycle.   Approximately half way through the ride cycle turn the main  power off to simulate a power failure. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: The capsule should slowly return to the rest or home position.  | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name:  Once the simulator has returned to the rest position test  the emergency valves on the air locker to open the door.  | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name:  Close the door, turn on electrical power and start up the system as per normal operating procedure. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name:  Lubricate door cylinder pivot points with a general purpose lubricating oil. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: If any issues were noted please create a support REQUEST in UpKeep regarding this issue. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Additional comments can be noted here. | Type: Text Form Item | Value: NONE;

Name: Review Weekly I360 Maintenance Checklists. (Attach pictures of weekly sheets to this item using the attachment or camera button to the right) | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Remove Nose and Tail Covers   | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Roll machine in both directions several times to inspect the timing belt for proper tension & tracking. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Be sure to turn off power and "LOCKOUT" the machine before performing any maintenance to mechanical systems. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Thoroughly inspect the roll lock mechanism to be sure it is sufficiently greased and that there is nothing restricting the movement of the pawl. (if applicable) | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Thoroughly inspect the roll lock pawl and spring for wear. (if applicable) | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check to ensure that the roll brake is functioning properly, adjust if required. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check for excessive backlash (play) between the roll gearbox and roll brake transition. (separate if necessary) | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Test roll brake manual release mechanism for proper functionality. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Inspect and test the functionality of the "Roll Arrestor" assembly. Check to ensure all fasteners are tight. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Check oil level in the pitch gearbox and inspect pitch linkage assembly. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: "One pump from the grease gun to the  following grease fittings.   (2) - roll pillow blocks              (2) - pitch pillow blocks       (2) - fittings at pitch linkage assembly (if applicable)   | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: With a rag remove the excess grease from all bearings and greasing points. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Thoroughly vacuum all electronic components on the entire machine including drives, braking resistors, wiring harnesses, etc.  Vacuum machine base and cradle frames during this step also. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Inspect control rack wiring to make sure all connections are secure and that all wiring is neatly routed. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Inspect all control rack components to be sure that everything is secure and all screws are in place. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Visually inspect capsule wiring for loose and frayed wires. Make sure all wiring & harnesses are secure. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Visually inspect seatbelts for signs of wear or malfunction. Ensure all fasteners are tight | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
Name: Thoroughly vacuum the rear of the capsule being sure to remove dust from amp, power supply, capsule wiring harnesses and fans. | Type: Task | Value: Complete;
Name: Visually inspect the condition of the capsule interior for poor housekeeping and damaged upholstery. | Type: Checklist Form Item | Value: Pass;
